						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 4: GRADIENT MODES\n\nThe Gradient node has two modes: Smooth and Stepped.\nSo far we've been looking at smooth, which is the default.\nStepped will turn the gradient into discrete colored steps.\nThe range of the steps runs from 2 to 512 (we've limited it to 12 in this example).\n\nDo note that when you switch from stepped to smooth, the steps inlet disapears. \nThis is something to take into consideration when creating patches that are used in Avenue\/Arena.\nBy design Arena\/Avenue can't break connections in Wire patches.\nIf we were to save this patch, we would see the buttons, but smooth would do nothing.\nThis is because selecting smooth would disconnect steps, which we don't allow Arena\/Avenue to do."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 790.96527099609375,
					"width": 697.13134765625,
					"x": -453.07666015625,
					"y": -296.656982421875
				},
